title: Cabinet Reshuffle
subtitle: Reopen every portfolio—or leave the cabinet untouched.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_government_card
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and government_has_confidence = 1 and caretaker_government = 0 and ministries_finalized = 1 and ministry_count >= 1 and month_actions < max_month_actions and poland_cabinet_reshuffle_timer <= 0
on-arrival: poland_cabinet_reshuffle_timer = 6
card-image: img/poland/cards/reshuffle.webp

= Cabinet Reshuffle

Six months of government have changed the price of every office. KO wants its
senior ministries back, PSL wants Agriculture and Defence treated as natural
property, and Lewica now knows which nameplates carry authority. A reshuffle
can reopen the whole cabinet table; declining it costs no action.

- @renegotiate
- @delivery_letters
- @keep

@renegotiate
title: Reopen the whole portfolio table
subtitle: Spend this month's action and conduct a live cabinet negotiation.
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; ministry_allocation_mode = "reshuffle"; ministry_return_mode = "card_finish"; ministry_reshuffle_previous_count = ministry_count; news_headline = "Lewica reopens every cabinet portfolio for negotiation"
go-to: poland_ministries


@delivery_letters
title: Keep the ministers and impose public delivery letters
subtitle: Spend this month's action on accountability without trading offices.
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; government_delivery += 2; public_trust += 2; government_coalition_dissent += 1; news_headline = "Cabinet ministers receive public one-hundred-day delivery letters"

No office changes hands. Each minister receives a short list of dated
commitments, allowing the next reshuffle argument to begin with a record
rather than rumours passed between coalition leaders.

- #poland_card_finish


@keep
title: Keep the cabinet exactly as it is
subtitle: No action, resource or budget cost. Close the conversation.
go-to: poland_hub
